IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`
IMPORT `cda-s10-interpretation`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, section 10: TESTS.
-- Layer 1 tests. Every expected value below was written from the section's text
-- before the file was run, and is stated in the comment above its assertion.
-- A failing assertion here would be a finding, not a value to be edited.

§ `Tests for section 10`

§§ `Fixtures: things`

`an ordinary tangible thing` MEANS Thing WITH
    `of a tangible nature` IS TRUE
    `money` IS FALSE
    `a wild creature tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity` IS FALSE
    `any other wild creature, or the carcass of a wild creature` IS FALSE
    `reduced into possession which has not been lost or abandoned` IS FALSE
    `in the course of being reduced into possession` IS FALSE
    `a mushroom, including any fungus, growing wild on any land` IS FALSE
    `flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant, including a shrub or tree, growing wild on any land` IS FALSE

`money` MEANS Thing WITH
    `of a tangible nature` IS FALSE
    `money` IS TRUE
    `a wild creature tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity` IS FALSE
    `any other wild creature, or the carcass of a wild creature` IS FALSE
    `reduced into possession which has not been lost or abandoned` IS FALSE
    `in the course of being reduced into possession` IS FALSE
    `a mushroom, including any fungus, growing wild on any land` IS FALSE
    `flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant, including a shrub or tree, growing wild on any land` IS FALSE

`something not of a tangible nature` MEANS Thing WITH
