§§ `Fixtures: one person's connection with property`

`a person with no connection` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS FALSE
    `interest in it` IS `no proprietary right or interest`
    `a charge on it` IS FALSE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS FALSE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS FALSE

`a person with custody or control` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS TRUE
    `interest in it` IS `no proprietary right or interest`
    `a charge on it` IS FALSE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS FALSE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS FALSE

`a person with a proprietary right or interest` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS FALSE
    `interest in it` IS `a proprietary right or interest`
    `a charge on it` IS FALSE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS FALSE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS FALSE

`a person with only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS FALSE
    `interest in it` IS `only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest`
    `a charge on it` IS FALSE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS FALSE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS FALSE

`a person with a charge on it` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS FALSE
    `interest in it` IS `no proprietary right or interest`
    `a charge on it` IS TRUE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS FALSE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS FALSE

`a person with a right to enforce a trust` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS FALSE
    `interest in it` IS `no proprietary right or interest`
    `a charge on it` IS FALSE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS TRUE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS FALSE

`a corporation sole whose property it is, with the office vacant` MEANS Connection WITH
    `custody or control of it` IS FALSE
    `interest in it` IS `no proprietary right or interest`
    `a charge on it` IS FALSE
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS FALSE
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS TRUE

§§ `Fixtures: property and who is connected with it`

`an ordinary thing that another has custody of` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with custody or control`

`an ordinary thing that nobody but the accused is connected with` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with custody or control`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS EMPTY

`an ordinary thing that the accused and another both have custody of` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with custody or control`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with custody or control`

`an ordinary thing in which another has only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest`

`a wild mushroom that another has custody of` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `a mushroom growing wild on land`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with custody or control`

`an ordinary thing that another has a proprietary interest in` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with a proprietary right or interest`

`an ordinary thing that another has a charge on` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with a charge on it`

`an ordinary thing that another can enforce a trust over` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with a right to enforce a trust`

`an ordinary thing that a vacant corporation sole owns` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a corporation sole whose property it is, with the office vacant`

`an ordinary thing that several unconnected persons and one with custody are linked to` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `a person with no connection`, `a person with no connection`, `a person with custody or control`

`an ordinary thing that nobody is connected with` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
    `the thing` IS `an ordinary tangible thing`
    `the accused's connection with it` IS `a person with no connection`
    `other persons' connections with it` IS EMPTY

§§ `Fixtures: what is done to the property`

`ordinary destruction or damage` MEANS Damage WITH
    `destruction or damage` IS TRUE
    `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS FALSE
    `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS FALSE

`no destruction or damage` MEANS Damage WITH
    `destruction or damage` IS FALSE
    `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS FALSE
    `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS FALSE

`a modification of the contents of a computer alone, with no effect on its physical condition` MEANS Damage WITH
    `destruction or damage` IS TRUE
    `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS TRUE
    `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS FALSE

`a modification of the contents of a computer that impairs its physical condition` MEANS Damage WITH
    `destruction or damage` IS TRUE
    `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS TRUE
    `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS TRUE

`an impairment of physical condition where the damage was not a modification of contents` MEANS Damage WITH
    `destruction or damage` IS TRUE
    `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS FALSE
    `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS TRUE

§§ `10(1): property -- every branch`

-- s 10(1): property of a tangible nature. Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `an ordinary tangible thing`

-- s 10(1): "including money". Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `money`

-- s 10(1): not of a tangible nature and not money. Expected: not property.
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is property within section 10(1)` `something not of a tangible nature`)

-- s 10(1)(a): a wild creature that has been tamed. Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `a tamed wild creature`

-- s 10(1)(a): a wild creature ordinarily kept in captivity. Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `a wild creature ordinarily kept in captivity`

-- s 10(1)(a): another wild creature reduced into possession (not lost or abandoned). Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `another wild creature, reduced into possession`

-- s 10(1)(a): another wild creature in the course of being reduced into possession. Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `another wild creature, in the course of being reduced into possession`

-- s 10(1)(a): "if, but only if" -- another wild creature neither reduced nor being reduced. Expected: NOT property, although it is tangible.
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is property within section 10(1)` `another wild creature, not reduced into possession (or the possession lost or abandoned)`)

-- s 10(1)(a): the carcass of a wild creature, reduced into possession. Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `the carcass of a wild creature, reduced into possession`

-- s 10(1)(a): the carcass of a wild creature, not reduced into possession. Expected: NOT property.
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is property within section 10(1)` `the carcass of a wild creature, not reduced into possession`)

-- s 10(1)(b): a mushroom (which includes any fungus) growing wild on land. Expected: NOT property.
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is property within section 10(1)` `a mushroom growing wild on land`)

-- s 10(1)(b): flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant (which includes a shrub or tree) growing wild on land. Expected: NOT property.
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is property within section 10(1)` `flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant growing wild on land`)

-- s 10(1)(b) excludes only WILD flowers and the rest: flowers of a cultivated plant are tangible. Expected: property.
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `flowers of a cultivated plant`

-- s 10(1)(b) names mushrooms and flowers, fruit and foliage, not the plant: a wild tree itself is tangible and not excluded. Expected: property (NOTES.md finding).
#ASSERT `a thing is property within section 10(1)` `a wild tree itself, not its flowers, fruit or foliage`

§§ `10(2) to (4): belonging`

-- s 10(2): a person with no connection. Expected: the property does not belong to that person.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a person with no connection`)

-- s 10(2)(a): custody or control. Expected: belongs.
#ASSERT `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a person with custody or control`

-- s 10(2)(b): a proprietary right or interest. Expected: belongs.
#ASSERT `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a person with a proprietary right or interest`

-- s 10(2)(b) bracket: an equitable interest arising ONLY from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest does not count. Expected: does not belong.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a person with only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest`)

-- s 10(2)(c): a charge on it. Expected: belongs.
#ASSERT `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a person with a charge on it`

-- s 10(3): a person with a right to enforce the trust to which the property is subject. Expected: belongs.
#ASSERT `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a person with a right to enforce a trust`

-- s 10(4): a corporation sole, notwithstanding a vacancy. Expected: belongs.
#ASSERT `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` `a corporation sole whose property it is, with the office vacant`

§§ `Property belonging to another, and to the accused`

-- s 10(1)+(2): ordinary thing, another has custody. Expected: belongs to another.
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that another has custody of`

-- Same. Expected: does not belong to the accused (no connection).
#ASSERT NOT (`property belonging to the accused` `an ordinary thing that another has custody of`)

-- Accused alone connected. Expected: does not belong to another.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that nobody but the accused is connected with`)

-- Accused alone connected. Expected: belongs to the accused.
#ASSERT `property belonging to the accused` `an ordinary thing that nobody but the accused is connected with`

-- s 10(2) "any person": property can belong to several persons. Accused and another both have custody. Expected: belongs to another AND to the accused (NOTES.md fork F4).
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that the accused and another both have custody of`

-- Same. Expected: belongs to the accused.
#ASSERT `property belonging to the accused` `an ordinary thing that the accused and another both have custody of`

-- Another has only an equitable interest from an agreement. Expected: does not belong to another.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing in which another has only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement`)

-- A wild mushroom is not property, so nothing belongs to anyone under the Act. Expected: not property belonging to another.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belonging to another` `a wild mushroom that another has custody of`)

-- Another has a proprietary interest. Expected: belongs to another.
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that another has a proprietary interest in`

-- Another has a charge on it. Expected: belongs to another.
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that another has a charge on`

-- Another can enforce the trust. Expected: belongs to another.
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that another can enforce a trust over`

-- A vacant corporation sole owns it. Expected: belongs to another.
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that a vacant corporation sole owns`

-- Only the third of three other persons has a connection. Expected: belongs to another (any one suffices).
#ASSERT `property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that several unconnected persons and one with custody are linked to`

-- Nobody is connected. Expected: does not belong to another.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belonging to another` `an ordinary thing that nobody is connected with`)

-- Nobody is connected. Expected: does not belong to the accused either.
#ASSERT NOT (`property belonging to the accused` `an ordinary thing that nobody is connected with`)

§§ `10(5): computers`

-- Ordinary destruction or damage. Expected: counts.
#ASSERT `destruction or damage within the Act` `ordinary destruction or damage`

-- No destruction or damage at all. Expected: does not count.
#ASSERT NOT (`destruction or damage within the Act` `no destruction or damage`)

-- s 10(5): a modification of the contents of a computer alone, with no effect on its physical condition. Expected: not damage.
#ASSERT NOT (`destruction or damage within the Act` `a modification of the contents of a computer alone, with no effect on its physical condition`)

-- s 10(5): a modification of the contents that impairs the physical condition. Expected: counts.
#ASSERT `destruction or damage within the Act` `a modification of the contents of a computer that impairs its physical condition`

-- s 10(5) bites only on a modification of contents: damage that is not one counts when the damage is there. Expected: counts.
#ASSERT `destruction or damage within the Act` `an impairment of physical condition where the damage was not a modification of contents`
